 a pawn down (−0.75)."},{"ply":34,"name":"17…Ncd3","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"17…Ncd3 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 68% to 49%.","points":["White answers 18.Nxf5, which takes the bishop on f5.","Better was 17…Bd3 (−2.05), which attacks the rook on f1."],"better":"17…Bd3 threatens …Bxf1, winning the exchange. Engine line: 18.Nce2 Qe7 19.h4 Na2 20.Rb1 c6 (−2.05)."},{"ply":35,"name":"18.Nxf5","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"18.Nxf5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the bishop on f5.","Shores up the e3 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (1 against 1).","The next best move, 18.Qd2, would drop White's winning chances from 51% to 34% (−1.83).","18.Nxf5 stops …Nxc1.","Black was threatening …Nxc1, winning the exchange. Nxf5 takes care of it.","Black answers 18…gxf5, winning the exchange."]},{"ply":41,"name":"21.Bb2","cls":"mistake","color":"w","headline":"21.Bb2 is a mistake: White's winning chances go from 46% to 36%.","points":["Black answers 21…Na2.","Better was 21.Na4 (−0.45): moving away uncovers the bishop on a1, which now hits the bishop on g7."],"better":"21.Na4 threatens Qxb4, winning a knight and a pawn. After 21…Na6 22.Bxg7 Kxg7 23.b4 Qf6 24.Nb6, the bishops are traded (−0.45)."},{"ply":44,"name":"22…Qa5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"22…Qa5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Adds a decisive attacker on the knight on c3: 3 attackers against 2 defenders.","Lines up queen and rook on the a-file, so the two pieces push in the same direction.","The next best move, 22…Nxc3, would drop Black's winning chances from 76% to 61% (−1.20).","22…Qa5 adds pressure on the knight on c3 and lines up queen and rook on the a-file.","Shores up the knight on a2, which was under as much attack as it had defence (1 against 1).","White answers 23.Ne2, uncovering an attack on the bishop on g7."]},{"ply":46,"name":"23…Qxd2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"23…Qxd2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the queen on d2.","Protects the d6 pawn, which was hanging.","The next best move, 23…Re6, would drop Black's winning chances from 77% to 63% (−1.46).","23…Qxd2 trades off the attacked queen instead of losing it to Qxa5 and trades queens.","White was threatening Qxa5, winning a pawn. The queen takes something with it instead.","Trades queens: the queens come off while ahead, which makes the extra material easier to convert."]},{"ply":48,"name":"24…Bxb2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"24…Bxb2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Takes the bishop on b2.","The next best move, 24…Be5, would drop Black's winning chances from 77% to 65% (−1.70).","24…Bxb2 trades off the attacked bishop instead of losing it to Bxg7 and trades bishops.","White was threatening Bxg7, winning a pawn. The bishop takes something with it instead.","Trades bishops: trading pieces when ahead brings the win closer.","The bishop on b2 can be taken by the rook on d2."]},{"ply":50,"name":"25…Nb4","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"25…Nb4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Shores up the c6 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (1 against 1).","The next best move, 25…Ra3, would drop Black's winning chances from 78% to 66% (−1.81).","25…Nb4 prepares …Ra2 and shores up the c6 pawn.","It prepares …Ra2: the knight covers a2.","White answers 26.Bf1.","Engine line: 26.Bf1 Ra2 27.Rb1 Rea8 28.Rd1 d5 (−3.37)."]}],"opening":{"name":"King's Indian Defense: Fianchetto Variation, Immediate Fianchetto","eco":"E60","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 7…Re8: 14 moves in all, 7 by White and 7 by Black.","Theory runs out after 7…Re8: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}